        "title": "Holy Roman Empire - The Bewildering Fragmentation",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nNOT HOLY:\n  The Pope crowned the emperor, but popes and emperors spent\n  centuries fighting each other (Investiture Controversy, Guelphs/\n  Ghibellines, Frederick II vs multiple popes).\n  \"Holy\" referred to the concept of a divinely sanctioned\n  Christian universal monarchy — the emperor as secular protector\n  of Christendom. In practice: anything but harmonious."
    },
    {
      "id": "04-HOLY-ROMAN-EMPIRE.md#004",
      "path": [
        "04-HOLY-ROMAN-EMPIRE.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:historical-geography:04-holy-roman-empire, git-history:historical-geography:04-holy-roman-empire]",
        "canonical_path": "historical-geography/04-HOLY-ROMAN-EMPIRE.md",
        "concepts": "[holy, roman, empire]",
        "current_path": "historical-geography/04-HOLY-ROMAN-EMPIRE.md",
        "id": "maxim:historical-geography:holy-roman-empire",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "historical-geography",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[holy, roman]",
        "section": "historical-geography",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Holy Roman Empire - The Bewildering Fragmentation",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "NOT ROMAN:\n  It was German. Based in German-speaking lands.\n  The \"Roman\" claim derived from Charlemagne's coronation 800 CE\n  by Pope Leo III — who was trying to create a Western counterpart\n  to the Byzantine (actual Roman) Empire.\n  Emperors went to Rome for coronation, but ruled from Frankfurt,\n  Aachen, Prague, Vienna, etc."
    },
    {
      "id": "04-HOLY-ROMAN-EMPIRE.md#005",
      "path": [
        "04-HOLY-ROMAN-EMPIRE.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:historical-geography:04-holy-roman-empire, git-history:historical-geography:04-holy-roman-empire]",
