        "id": "maxim:historical-geography:holy-roman-empire",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "historical-geography",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[holy, roman]",
        "section": "historical-geography",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Holy Roman Empire - The Bewildering Fragmentation",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "NOT AN EMPIRE:\n  An empire implies a single sovereign power over a territory.\n  The HRE was a confederation of princes who elected a chairman.\n  The emperor couldn't tax them directly, couldn't legislate\n  without their consent, couldn't raise an army without their\n  cooperation."
    },
    {
      "id": "04-HOLY-ROMAN-EMPIRE.md#006",
      "path": [
        "04-HOLY-ROMAN-EMPIRE.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
