      },
      "text": "Otto I established the **Ottonian system**: appointing bishops and abbots as royal administrators. Clergy couldn't pass fiefs to children (celibacy), so ecclesiastical lords' territories reverted to royal control for re-appointment. This gave the king a powerful tool — and planted the seed of the Investiture Crisis."
    },
