      "text": "1073: Gregory VII becomes Pope; launches Gregorian Reform\n  1075: Gregory bans lay investiture (emperor appointing bishops)\n  1076: Henry IV convenes council at Worms; \"deposes\" Gregory\n        Gregory excommunicates Henry; releases his vassals from oaths\n  1077: Walk to Canossa\n        Henry stands barefoot in snow for 3 days outside the castle\n        Gregory must lift excommunication (canonical obligation)\n        Henry survives; vassals return\n        → Gregory had not really won\n  1080: Henry IV drives Gregory out of Rome; Gregory dies in exile\n  1122: Concordat of Worms (under Henry V): the compromise\n        (see 01-FEUDAL-MECHANICS.md for details)\n```"
    },
