      "text": "**Frederick II** (r. 1220–1250): \"Stupor Mundi\" — Wonder of the World\n```\nWHAT MADE HIM EXTRAORDINARY:\n  - Born in Sicily; raised there; native Arabic, German, French, Latin, Italian, Greek\n  - Built Castel del Monte (Sicily) — geometric perfection, no clear military purpose\n  - Wrote poetry in Italian (predates Dante)\n  - Wrote scientific treatise on falconry (De Arte Venandi cum Avibus)\n  - Negotiated Jerusalem via diplomacy (Sixth Crusade 1229):\n    Treaty with al-Kamil (Ayyubid sultan) — Christians get Jerusalem\n    without fighting — Pope furious (it was too rational)\n  - Fought three popes (Gregory IX twice, Innocent IV)\n  - Excommunicated multiple times\n  - Created the most sophisticated royal bureaucracy in 13th century Europe\n    in Sicily (centralized, salaried officials, no feudal intermediaries)"
    },
